questions.question:
What does this print?
for i in range(3):
    print(i)
else:
    print("done")

What does this print?
for i in range(3):
    if i == 1:
        break
    print(i)
else:
    print("done")

questions.answer:
break at i == 1 means the loop was interrupted, so the else does NOT run and only 0 prints.

code:
for i in range(3):
    if i == 1:
        break
    print(i)
else:
    print("done")

