questions.question:
What does this print?
for i in range(3):
    if i:
        print(i)

What does this print?
for i in range(3):
    for j in range(3):
        if j == 2:
            break
        print(i, j)

questions.answer:
The inner loop breaks at j == 2 each round, so every row prints only (i,0) and (i,1).

code:
for i in range(3):
    for j in range(3):
        if j == 2:
            break
        print(i, j)

